      "audience": "Narrative designers, content strategists, prompt authors",
      "rationale": "Why it matters: When a source contains mixed emphases, generic preservation instructions may latch onto whichever element appears strongest in Synthesis; resolving or disambiguating internal tensions in the Synthesis may be necessary before adding reusable preservation rules. Gaps and uncertainty: the causal link is presented as a plausible amplification ('may have reinforced')—the experiment documents correlation (baseline ambiguity and candidate drift) but does not prove causation.",
      "evidence": "Report states: 'The baseline Synthesis pairs company identity with Compose in its top-level emphasis, but also contains a later description calling orchestration “central to the product direction.” That internal tension may have reinforced the technical angle.' Candidate outputs made orchestration central across runs."
